{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.UnitalGroebnerBasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UnitalGroebnerBasesChapter.UnitalGroebnerBasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WellFounded","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.value","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The S-polynomial value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.f'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.f'","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Second element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.f","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.f","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L68-L68","doc":"First element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.SPolynomial","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L60-L72","doc":"An **S-polynomial** about f, f' ∈ A is constructible when their\nleading terms can be aligned:\nλ · LT(u · LT(f) · v) = λ' · LT(u' · LT(f') · v')\n\nThe S-polynomial is then: S(f, f') = λu·f·v − λ'u'·f'·v' ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital.product_lc_units","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital.product_lc_units","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Products preserve the unit leading coefficient property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital.lc_units","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital.lc_units","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Leading coefficients of generators are units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.IsUnital","kind":"structure","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L47-L57","doc":"The **unital condition** on a Gröbner basis:\n1. All generators have leading coefficient in R×\n2. All products α · g · β have leading coefficient in R× (when nonzero)\n\nOver a field, every Gröbner basis is automatically unital. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.has_representation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.has_representation","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Every element of the ideal has a Gröbner representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.ideal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.ideal","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The two-sided ideal generated by the generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.generators","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The generating set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.UnitalGroebner.GroebnerBasis","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/unital-groebner-basis.lean#L29-L43","doc":"A **Gröbner basis** G for a two-sided ideal I with respect to\nan admissible system (B, <).\n\nG is a Gröbner basis if every h ∈ I has a representation\nh = Σ_k λ_k · u_k · g_{γ_k} · v_k with controlled leading monomials. ","signatureChunk":0}]}